==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Teutonick]]

===Etymology===
1580, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|Teutōnicus}}, from {{term/t|la|Teutōnes}}, {{term|Teutōnī||the Teutons|tr=name of a Germanic tribe that inhabited coastal Germany and devastated Gaul between 113-101 B.C.|lang=la}}. See {{term|Teuton|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌtjuːˈtɒn.ɪk/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/%tju:"tQn.Ik/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒnɪk}}

